Usage:
  x2c <command> [options]

x2c translates x2c source to C and can optionally compile and link the
result with the host C toolchain.

Commands:

  translate   Translate .x files to .c and .h files
  build       Translate, compile, and optionally link a target
  run         Build an executable and run it
  bootstrap   Install a native x2c from a APE binary
  help        Show help for x2c or one command

Global options:
  -h, --help                  Show help and exit
  -V, --version               Show the x2c version and exit
  -v, --verbose               Show commands as they are executed
  -q, --quiet                 Suppress successful progress and receipts
      --plain                 Use stable output without terminal rendering
      --color <auto|always|never>
                              Control terminal color
      --debug                 Enable compiler debug logging

Input syntax:

  @<file>                     Read additional arguments from a response file
  --                          End option parsing

Run 'x2c help <command>' or 'x2c <command> --help' for command help.
